node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store

# Deny everything env-shaped, then re-admit the documentation file. A narrower
# pattern lets copies through: a backup like .env.local.bak holds the same key
# as the original, and no secret may reach git.
.env*
!.env.example

# Run output IS tracked from here on, which reverses assumption A12 ("the
# repository is the code, the archive is what the code makes"). Deployment
# forced the change: GitHub Pages serves this branch's root, and every daily
# run happens on a fresh runner with no disk of its own. If the archive were
# not committed, each run would rebuild an index containing only that day's
# edition and every earlier page would vanish. Committing the output is what
# makes the archive an archive. Recorded as A33.
#
# state/seen.json is tracked for the same reason and matters more: it is the
# only record of what has already been published, so a runner that started
# without it would re-publish papers already covered. See A34 for how the
# commit-back handles a concurrent push.

logs/*.log

# Scratch output for local previewing. Never a deliverable.
tmp/

# Internal working notes. Kept out of the public repo pending Tom's review;
# they hold spend figures, candid product assessments and personal detail.
# To publish: remove this rule and `git add docs/`.
docs/
